# What this environment adds to the RAPIDS notebooks image, as direct
# requirements. `requirements.lock` beside this file is the resolved closure of
# these ten lines with a sha256 for every wheel, and the lock is what the
# container installs — this file exists so a reader can see what was asked for
# and regenerate the lock (charts/rapids-singlecell-notebook/README.md).
#
# Versions follow the blueprint's own requirements.txt wherever it pins one, so
# the environment a tenant gets is the environment the notebooks were written
# against. clickhouse-connect is ours: it is how the gated path reads a dataset
# the gatekeeper serves.
